## Day 6. Cloud and wiring (4 to 5 hrs)

- Export the CNN to ONNX (Phase 7) for the ONI forecast endpoint.
- S3: model, latest input, `forecast.json`, `oni_monthly.csv`.
- Lambda + API Gateway:
  - ONI forecast endpoint (ONNX), and/or
  - impacts endpoint (`cloud/lambda_impacts.py` — same live Open-Meteo path as local FastAPI).
- Wire the map to HTTPS endpoints so clicks and the ONI readout are cloud-backed.

**Done when:** deployed endpoints work over HTTPS and the map uses them.

**If behind:** host the static map on S3, keep FastAPI local for demo video; add Lambda in Stretch 1.

**Links:**
- ONNX export from PyTorch: https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/onnx.html
- onnxruntime: https://onnxruntime.ai/docs/
- Lambda with container images, avoids the size limit: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/python-image.html
- API Gateway plus Lambda tutorial: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-develop-integrations-lambda.html
- S3 static website hosting: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/WebsiteHosting.html

